===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|kërbe|t=incision, notch}}, from {{inh|de|goh|*kerba}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*kerbā}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*kerbǭ}}, related to {{m|gem-pro|*kerbaną|t=to cut, carve}}.

Cognate with {{cog|nds-de|Karve}}, {{cog|dum|kerve}}, {{cog|stq|Käärwe}}, {{cog|non|kjarf|t=bundle}}, {{cog|ang|cyrf|t=incision}} (whence {{cog|en|kerf}}).<ref>{{R:Kluge 1891|Kerbe}}</ref>

